{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01TrBnW1imm13FCNp6Zfgo1h", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.culture.ru/events/338705/prazdnik-spozhinki\"}, {\"url\": \"https://booksite.ru/fulltext/1/001/007/073/73268.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://booksite.ru/fulltext/zab/avy/vok/rug/pec/hky/13.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ruthenia.ru/folklore/folklorelaboratory/07sevzat.doc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://work.zabgu.ru/Faculties/FKiI/MUZ_17/%d0%9d%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%be%d0%b4%d0%bd%d0%be%d0%b5%20%d0%bc%d1%83%d0%b7%d1%8b%d0%ba%d0%b0%d0%bb%d1%8c%d0%bd%d0%be%d0%b5%20%d1%82%d0%b2%d0%be%d1%80%d1%87%d0%b5%d1%81%d1%82%d0%b2%d0%be/13.10%2020.doc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://vk.ru/@pk_museum-obzhinki1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bigenc.ru/c/zazhinki-3979a3\"}, {\"url\": \"https://inet.qq.com/read/1000810725/262\"}, {\"url\": \"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EjGFlUVR4PmZmspVi_PKFGg6ify5Vquu/export?format=pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:30:47.255Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"последний сноп\" \"молча\" \"именинник\" OR \"именинным\" жатва обряд", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01RF4eS45zyyxBPKssuYbshQ", "content": [{"title": "prazdnik spozhinki", "url": "https://www.culture.ru/events/338705/prazdnik-spozhinki"}, {"title": "booksite.ru", "url": "https://booksite.ru/fulltext/1/001/007/073/73268.htm"}, {"title": "booksite.ru", "url": "https://booksite.ru/fulltext/zab/avy/vok/rug/pec/hky/13.htm"}, {"title": "VII. СЕВ И ЖАТВА", "url": "https://www.ruthenia.ru/folklore/folklorelaboratory/07sevzat.doc"}, {"title": "Лабораторное занятие по Народному музыкальному творчеству", "url": "https://work.zabgu.ru/Faculties/FKiI/MUZ_17/%d0%9d%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%be%d0%b4%d0%bd%d0%be%d0%b5%20%d0%bc%d1%83%d0%b7%d1%8b%d0%ba%d0%b0%d0%bb%d1%8c%d0%bd%d0%be%d0%b5%20%d1%82%d0%b2%d0%be%d1%80%d1%87%d0%b5%d1%81%d1%82%d0%b2%d0%be/13.10%2020.doc"}, {"title": "@pk museum obzhinki1", "url": "https://vk.ru/@pk_museum-obzhinki1"}, {"title": "zazhinki 3979a3", "url": "https://bigenc.ru/c/zazhinki-3979a3"}, {"title": "inet.qq.com", "url": "https://inet.qq.com/read/1000810725/262"}, {"title": "docs.google.com", "url": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EjGFlUVR4PmZmspVi_PKFGg6ify5Vquu/export?format=pdf"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything that directly matches the combination of the last sheaf, silence, and a birthday person (именинник). The results cover related harvest-end rituals, so they're only a partial answer.\n\n- **Обжинки (harvest-end rite):** A booksite entry describes a custom where a woman weaves a wreath from ears of grain and carries it to the field owner with songs. Afterward, the wreath's grain was kept until the next sowing and scattered first. The owner, usually a landlord in older times, treated the reapers to vodka, and the wreath was saved until the nearest sowing. The same entry says at the end of the harvest, a handful of uncut grain is left, tied into a bundle and decorated with flowers, which is the closest match to the sheaf custom, though it doesn't mention silence or a birthday.\n- **Обжинки as a whole:** One museum source defines it as a day of the Slavic folk calendar and a rite marking the end of the grain harvest, and says it was held at different times depending on climate and region.\n- **Зажинки (harvest-start rite):** The Great Russian Encyclopedia describes these as a set of ritual actions tied to the start of the harvest among Slavic peoples. Its entry also notes that participants were supposed to go to the field quickly, and leave quickly once the rite was finished, ideally unnoticed by others, which is the nearest thing to the \"silent\" element, though it refers to the start of harvest rather than its end.\n\nNothing in these results mentions a birthday person (именинник) receiving the last sheaf. The custom may be regional or documented in ethnographic monographs not indexed here. A narrower search on a regional name, or on \"последний сноп\" with \"именинник\" in an ethnographic journal, would be the next step."], "durationSeconds": 6.537780417, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01TrBnW1imm13FCNp6Zfgo1h", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
